enable-vendor-permanent-auth: enable VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE (TPM_RH_AUTH_00)

Classification: profile setting.

tpm-rs implements the vendor permanent authorization handle TPM_RH_AUTH_00,
so the reference enables it as well. It relies on fix-startup-get-unique-
auth.patch (to build and to load the value), fix-vendor-auth-entity-
break.patch (to use it) and platform-vendor-unique-value.patch (tpm-rs's value).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
--- a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
@@ -199,10 +199,10 @@
 //***********************************************
 // Enable VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE?
 //***********************************************
-#define VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_ENABLED       NO
+#define VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_ENABLED       YES
 // if YES, this must be valid per Part2 (TPM_RH_AUTH_00 - TPM_RH_AUTH_FF)
 // if NO, this must be #undef
-#undef  VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE
+#define VENDOR_PERMANENT_AUTH_HANDLE        TPM_RH_AUTH_00
 
 //***********************************************
 // Defines controlling optional implementation
